Data and text adapted from AgentDojo (MIT)
------------------------------------------

AgentDojo: https://github.com/ethz-spylab/agentdojo
Copyright (c) 2024 Edoardo Debenedetti, Jie Zhang, Mislav Balunovic,
Luca Beurer-Kellner, Marc Fischer, and Florian Tramèr.
Licensed under the MIT License; the full text is in
third_party/agentdojo/LICENSE.

Adapted, with modifications, in MoonBit:

- suites/banking/env.mbt: the banking environment (account, transactions,
  scheduled transactions, files, user profile);
- suites/banking/tasks.mbt: the banking user tasks and injection tasks
  (prompts and success criteria) and the "important_instructions" attack
  text;
- suites/banking/spec.mbt and suites/banking/tools.mbt: the banking tool
  names, parameters and descriptions, and the behaviour of the tools;
- suites/mail/data.mbt, suites/mail/env.mbt and suites/mail/spec.mbt: the
  inbox, tools and e-mail tasks of the workspace suite;
- web/scenarios.mbt: playground scenarios built on that data.


Ideas and annotations from CaMeL (Apache-2.0)
---------------------------------------------

CaMeL: "Defeating Prompt Injections by Design", E. Debenedetti et al., 2025.
Reference implementation: https://github.com/google-research/camel-prompt-injection
Copyright 2025 Google LLC. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Bactrian re-implements CaMeL's ideas (the privileged/quarantined LLM split,
capability labels with sources and readers, per-tool security policies, the
`query_ai_assistant` interface with its `have_enough_information` flag) from
scratch in MoonBit. No CaMeL source code is copied.

One part is a translation rather than a re-implementation: the security
annotations of the banking tools in suites/banking/tools.mbt (who wrote each
part of a tool's result and who may read it) and the banking policy in
suites/banking/spec.mbt were translated from CaMeL's AgentDojo annotations
(src/camel/pipeline_elements/agentdojo_function.py) and banking policy
(src/camel/pipeline_elements/security_policies/banking.py), with
modifications: file contents are labelled public rather than private, a
payee taken from data asks for confirmation instead of being denied, and the
rules are written in Bactrian's policy language.
